[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113465,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 59,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Intercalated duct adenoma and hyperplasia are benign salivary ductal proliferations resembling bilayered (epithelial and myoepithelial) intercalated ducts.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113466,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 59,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113467,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 59,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E91.Z Benign neoplasm of unspecified major salivary glands</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113468,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 59,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> adenomatous ductal proliferation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113469,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 59,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113470,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 59,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The majority (85%) of cases arise in the parotid gland, followed by the submandibular gland (11%) and the oral cavity (4%) {7868091; 10971702; 11174600; 12072816; 19542868; 22271513; 22460810; 25497834}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113471,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 59,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most cases are incidental, identified concurrently with other salivary gland lesions (e.g. basal cell adenoma, epithelial-myoepithelial carcinoma) {10971702; 19542868; 24299520; 25497834}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113472,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 59,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Intercalated duct adenoma and hyperplasia are rarely reported {7868091; 10971702; 11174600; 12072816; 19542868; 22271513; 22460810; 24299520; 25497834}. There is an M:F&nbsp;ratio of 2:3, occurring in middle age (mean age: 52&nbsp;years).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113473,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 59,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113474,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 59,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "<p >Adenomas have been shown to harbour hotspot <em>HRAS</em> pathogenic variants, while hyperplasia often has <em>CTNNB1</em> mutations {36480093}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-22T14:17:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113475,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 59,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Intercalated duct adenoma and hyperplasia are rarely detected macroscopically. Most lesions are &lt;&nbsp;5&nbsp;mm {19542868}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113476,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 59,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "<p>Intercalated duct lesions manifest as a nodular, occasionally multinodular, proliferation of cuboidal ductal cells with attenuated myoepithelial cells, sometimes containing acinic cells. Intercalated duct lesions are subdivided into adenoma when well circumscribed or encapsulated, and hyperplasia when blending with adjacent acini {19542868; 36480093}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>If well circumscribed, it should be distinguished from striated duct adenoma (which lacks myoepithelial cells) {19542868; 21054495}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T14:45:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113477,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 59,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Smears show cohesive large tissue fragments of epithelial cells with high N:C&nbsp;ratios and bland oval nuclei, with admixed thin stromal strands {26477034}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113478,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 59,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113479,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 59,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a monotonous proliferation of cuboidal ductal cells surrounded by myoepithelial cells, sometimes with acinic cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113480,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 59,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113481,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 59,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most are incidental lesions, with an excellent prognosis.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]